A||||4||AkursedX||Oil Pressure Question||||1||
Z||000000||AkursedX||10-28-2001||04:53 PM||||Well my 87GT is just about all done and it'll be on the road next week!!<P>But I would like to know if this problem is something I should be wary of...<P>Now, when I bought this car, it leaked oil terribly from the sending unit, so I changed it and I have no more leak.  I am also using 10w30 oil in it.  And it also has 83k miles.<P>Now, when I start the car up, the oil pressure is nice and high but as it warms up, it drops significantly (like almost down to the red zone when it's hot) at idle, but when I give it gas, it'll shoot right up to above the 1/2way point.  Is this a sign of a failing oil pump??  Or is it ok?  I know I should get the oil pressure checked on a spereate guage but I just haven't had the time to.<P>The reason this worries me is that my 88GT never drops below the 1/2way mark even when it's warm, but it is running with 15w50 oil, so that might be the reason<P>Any feedback would be appreciated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||10-28-2001||06:26 PM||||the heavier oil is part of it. No 2 cars will operate with same oil pressures at all times. Anything above the red zone is fine for idle, and when its hot and been running a while anything constant over 35 or 40 pnds is ok. Ive noticed too that mine drops a little when the oil needs changed (handy reminder to me) and I use synthetic. I have hi performance oil pump and it carries 45-50 at idle and 65-70 running. Any engine rebuilds, I recommend the swap, its only slightly higher priced, direct bolt in.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-28-2001||07:14 PM||||Sounds like a normal worn engine. If it's above the red, keep drive. Likely lots of miles left. Just listen for the sounds of rocks rattling near the timing chain cover when it's cold. The chain will break soon after that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-28-2001||08:38 PM||||When I put the 3.4 in my car, I replaced the oil pump with a generic, "standard volume" pump. The engine only has about 80,000 miles on it, but at hot idle the pressure sits barely above the red and 40 psi at highway speeds. Before I get too concerned, I will hook a mechanical guage to the engine and see if the pressure is really that low. If it is that low, I am going to just get a 3.8 or 4.9 Caddy and stuff back there. The 3.4 is fun, but a rebuild would cost as much as a salvage yard replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000004||camon||10-28-2001||11:12 PM||||My oil pressure in my 87 GT is almost identical as you described yours as being...."high when cold, low (right around red) when warm and at idle, but comes upto 1/2 way (40psi, slightly above) when in motion. Well this had me concerned as well when I noticed it. Well after reading all I could on this topic i'm no longer concerned...because everything I read leads me to believe this is normal.<P>I looked in my Fiero owners manual and it states in there that normal oil pressure should be 20-60psi when engine is warm. If it falls below this (other then at idle) turn the engine off and investigate the cause. Flucuation is normal....it also says that oil pressure should not drop below 4psi even at an idle. So I don't think you have anything to worry about.....Mine is the same way!<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||12
